-- title:
--   The element V is a non-zero-divisor on the crossing model
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a commutative ring and let $\pi$ be an element of $W$ lying in the submonoid $\mathrm{nonZeroDivisors}\,W$, i.e. such that $w\pi = 0$ forces $w = 0$ for $w \in W$. Form the crossing model $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,\pi$, namely the quotient of the ring $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$ of formal power series in two variables over $W$ by the ideal generated by the single element $X_0 X_1 - C(\pi)$, where $C$ is the constant-coefficient inclusion $W \to \mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\,(\mathrm{Fin}\,2)\,W$. The assertion is that the element `V π` of this quotient ring is a non-zero-divisor: every $x$ in $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\,W\,\pi$ with $x \cdot (V\,\pi) = 0$ is zero. Here `V π` is the second of the two distinguished elements of the crossing model, characterised for the purposes of this statement by the relation $(U\,\pi)\cdot(V\,\pi) = \mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi$ recorded in [`ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.U_mul_V`](thm.html#ModularCurve.UVCrossingModel.U_mul_V), with $\mathrm{const}\,\pi\,\pi$ the image of $\pi$ in the quotient.
--
--   This is the second half of the statement that the two branch coordinates of the ordinary double point model $W[[u,v]]/(uv-\pi)$ are non-zero-divisors; for $W$ the Witt vectors of $\bar{\mathbb F}_p$ and $\pi$ a power of $p$ this ring is the completed local ring of the $\Gamma_0(p)$-moduli problem at a supersingular point. It is used in the analysis of local charts of the Drinfeld curve and in the classification of ring isomorphisms of crossing models that respect the distinguished elements.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_UVCrossingModel_V_mem_nonZeroDivisors.lean

